    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L16-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "16.3: Populations of Two Countries",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The population, in millions, of Country C is given by the equation \\(f(t) = 16 \\boldcdot e^{(0.02t)}\\). The population of Country D is given by \\(g(t) = 17.5 \\boldcdot e^{(0.025t)}\\). In both equations, \\(t\\) is the number of years since…",
