    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L16-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "16.3: Populations of Two Countries",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The population, in thousands, of a colony of carpenter ants and a colony of red wood ants can be modeled with functions \\(c(x) = 8.1 \\boldcdot e^{(0.03x)}\\) and \\(r(x)= 5.4 \\boldcdot e^{(0.05x)}\\), respectively. Here, \\(x\\) is the time in…",
